## Summary

I implemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year.

The project generates DTOs at build time via openapi-generator and maps them with MapStruct, and it already had a precedent for derived read-only fields (`initials`, `displayName`). I followed that same pattern:

1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** — Added a `readOnly` `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (example `'SMI-0007-M26'`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.

2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** — Added a derived getter:
   ```java
   public String getMembershipNumber() {
       if (this.customerCode == null || this.registrationDate == null) {
           return null;
       }
       return String.format("%s-M%02d", this.customerCode, this.registrationDate.getYear() % 100);
   }
   ```
   MapStruct auto-maps `getMembershipNumber()` → `setMembershipNumber()` by name, so no mapper change was needed. The `%02d` handling ensures a year like 2005 yields `M05`. It's derived purely from the owner's own fields (matching the `Cp14Tests` "seed-independent" note), and safely returns `null` if either source field is absent.

No new field is persisted — it's computed on read, consistent with how `customerCode`/`registrationDate` feed it.

